# Every setting Tamalou reads from its environment, with the value the code uses when it is unset.
# No key here is a secret: the defaults are already public (in the code, or in every built page).
#
# NOTHING LOADS THIS FILE, AND NOTHING LOADS A .env AT THE ROOT. Each part reads its settings its own way:
#   - Web build (Vite, `pnpm build` / `pnpm dev`): Vite's root is apps/web, so it loads apps/web/.env,
#     apps/web/.env.local and apps/web/.env.production, plus any VITE_* variable from the shell (the shell wins).
#     Copy the VITE_* lines there, or export them. A root .env is ignored (checked 2026-10-22).
#   - LAN server (apps/server/src/main.ts, `pnpm serve:lan`, the Docker image): reads process.env only and loads no
#     file. Export the variables, set them under `environment:` in docker-compose.yml, or start it with
#     `node --env-file=.env apps/server/src/main.ts`.
#   - Docker image: .dockerignore leaves every .env file out of the build and the Dockerfile passes no build argument,
#     so the image's web build always takes the defaults below. The Dockerfile sets NODE_ENV=production, PORT=8080 and
#     HOST=0.0.0.0; no code here reads NODE_ENV.
#   - Worker (apps/worker, online play): reads no variable. Its bindings (ROOMS, ASSETS, CREATE_LIMIT) are declared
#     in apps/worker/wrangler.jsonc.
#
# A line commented out has no value that means "unset": writing one would change what the code does.

# --- LAN server (apps/server/src/main.ts) -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Port the room server and the web app listen on.
PORT=8080
# Interface to listen on; 0.0.0.0 is every interface, and then the server prints each LAN address with a QR code.
HOST=0.0.0.0
# Folder of the built web app served next to the rooms. Unset: apps/web/dist next to the server (`pnpm build` first).
# An empty value is not "unset": it would serve nothing.
# WEB_DIR=/app/apps/web/dist
# Address phones should open, printed with its QR code instead of the machine's own addresses (Docker Desktop, where
# the container's address is useless to a phone), e.g. http://192.168.1.20:8080/. Empty: the detected addresses.
PUBLIC_URL=

# --- Web build (apps/web/build/site.ts, apps/web/build/analytics.ts; Vite loads them from apps/web/.env) -------------

# Canonical address the pages, social cards, robots.txt, the sitemap and llms.txt are written for. Empty or not an
# http(s) address: the default below.
VITE_SITE_URL=https://tamalou.steevepommier.com/
# Umami tracker (ADR-0018). Empty or not an http(s) address: the default below.
VITE_UMAMI_SRC=https://insight.steevepommier.com/insight
# Umami website id. Unset: the id in apps/web/build/site.ts (public, it is in every page). EMPTY TURNS MEASUREMENT OFF.
# VITE_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
# Hosts allowed to report, comma-separated. Unset: the build's own host (from VITE_SITE_URL) plus
# tamalou.steevepommier.com and costardrouge.github.io. A LAN server's host is never among them.
# VITE_UMAMI_DOMAINS=
# `true` writes the measurement settings into a dev build too (production builds only, otherwise).
VITE_UMAMI_DEV=false

# --- Tooling ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Chromium for apps/web/scripts/screenshots.ts (the install dialog's screenshots). Empty: Playwright's own browser.
CHROMIUM_PATH=

# --- Kept in GitHub's settings only, never in a file -----------------------------------------------------------------
# deploy.yml's Cloudflare job reads two values from the repository's settings (ADR-0014). They are listed for
# reference; a developer never fills them, and they never go in a .env:
#   CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN    secret (Settings → Secrets) — a token that can deploy Workers
#   CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID   variable (Settings → Variables) — the Cloudflare account; unset keeps the job off
